11103	11201	11095	11095	Luke	366	" Pshaw ! of what advantage is a dead hand ? ' Tis an unlucky keepsake , and will lead to mischief . The only use I ever heard of such a thing being turned to , was in the case of Bow - legged Ben , who was hanged in irons for murder , on Hardchase Heath , on the York Road , and whose hand was cut off at the wrist the first night to make a Hand of Glory , or Dead Man 's Candle . Hast never heard what the old song says ? "
