144070	144168	144067	144068	the count	4180	" was seldom used , except upon great emergencies , by any of the Stop Hole Abbey crew . It was a sort of retiring den of our old lioness Barbara , and , like all belonging to her , respected by her dupes . However , the cave is a good cave for all that ; is well concealed by brushwood , and comfortably lighted from a crevice in the rock above ; it lies near the brink of the stream , amongst the woods just above the waterfall , and is somewhat difficult of approach . "
